  "findings": [
    "Full rendering: 67\u201372 ms CPU. Cached parsing plus disabled event/machine wiring and markup validation: about 54 ms, retaining exact HTML only for this captured snapshot.",
    "Removing row attributes and custom renderer output as well reduces CPU to about 40 ms, with visibly incorrect output. This is an observed ablation result, not a universal rendering lower bound.",
    "Markup validation alone contributes little compared with the DOM pipeline; removing safety checks is not an attractive production optimization.",
    "Serialization of an already-built frozen DOM costs about 6 ms. Serving frozen HTML costs 0.7\u20130.8 ms. Neither performs dynamic rendering or proves freshness.",
    "The useful next production candidate is validated template preparation reused across requests, plus an explicit separation of SSR initialization from browser event wiring. A much larger reduction would require minimizing DOM allocation through a compiled rendering plan."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Replay queries contain pre-materialized tab-state and suppress writes; skipping machine wiring can appear correct because required work already happened during capture.",
    "Template cloning retains an original document and has not established ownership, invalidation, memory bounds, or correct behavior across changed data or templates.",
    "All cases use one Portuguese Flamengo route and captured data. No actual database, network reads, production Worker measurements, Container measurements or Lighthouse score.",
    "Static and serialization controls pay no query, binding or chart-generation cost. They do not demonstrate a sub-10-ms dynamic renderer.",
    "Local process CPU measured through ps has 10-ms total resolution; 300 requests were used for cheap controls. Runtime scheduling, JIT and GC still cause variation."
  ],
  "reproduce": [
    "Use pinned Deno 2.9.7 from apps/golaberto and Wrangler 4.149.0. Install the existing spike dependencies and obtain capture output as described in results.json.",
    "From apps/golaberto: mise exec -- deno run -A ../../plugins/omnishell/spikes/native-worker/prepare.ts <capture-directory>",
    "From apps/golaberto: mise exec -- deno run -A ../../plugins/omnishell/spikes/native-worker/floor-prepare.ts <capture-directory>",
    "From this spike directory, with ports 20218 and 20219 free: python3 floor-bench.py <absolute-wrangler-executable> <output-json>",
    "The generator writes separate patched modules/configuration under ignored .generated/. The ordinary worker.ts and interpreter sources are unchanged. Never deploy the floor configuration."
  ],
